# Golden retrieval judgments for boost's RAG engines.
# One JSON object per line: {query, relevant[], exemplar, kind, note}
#   query    - what a user might type
#   relevant - skill/rule/workflow name(s) the query is about, kept as prose:
#              every row now pins an exemplar, so this no longer decides grading
#   exemplar - "tap::skill_md", or a list of them, naming the BODY the query was
#              written about. Relevance is the content class of those bodies, so
#              a byte-identical mirror still counts and a different skill that
#              happens to share the name does not. A list is one class: any of
#              the pinned bodies is the right answer, not all of them.
#   kind     - the target's item kind (for per-kind metric slices)
# All 91 rows are pinned. scripts/eval_retrieval.py --worksheet reports 0 rows
# still graded by name, and prepare_row raises on a spec that resolves to no
# indexed entry, so a stale pin fails the gate rather than quietly weakening it.
